R[7]:
  Never run before testability is established; an unreadable game yields a confident wrong report
  Never let a bridge fabricate state; throwing on unimplemented methods is the correct behavior
  Keep game quality scores and test credibility diagnostics apart in every summary
  Initialize whole scenarios rather than single fields; partial jumps produce meaningless passes
  Score the feedback dimension only from player-observable response not internal API deltas
  Bind each merged problem to one best-attempt evidence set with a screenshot or a clip of at most 20 seconds
  State degradation explicitly for keyless runs missing source ZIPs single runs and unreached key nodes
